WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:08.180
A mouse lacking the NGF receptor is born with too few sympathetic neurons.

2
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:11.140
Were they never made, or made and then lost?

3
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.230
A knockout mouse has a gene disrupted, so it makes no working protein.

4
00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:18.570
No antibody is involved.

5
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.860
In 1994, Crowley and colleagues reported mice lacking NGF.

6
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:30.240
Smeyne, Klein, Barbacid and colleagues reported mice lacking a working TrkA, the

7
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.500
receptor for NGF.

8
00:00:32.583 --> 00:00:36.623
Both mutants lose sympathetic neurons and many sensory neurons.

9
00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:38.803
The antibody doubt is settled.

10
00:00:39.867 --> 00:00:45.247
The sensory losses fall on neurons that express TrkA, mostly small neurons that

11
00:00:45.247 --> 00:00:46.527
sense pain and temperature.

12
00:00:47.617 --> 00:00:51.377
But a count at birth still cannot say whether the neurons were ever made.

13
00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:59.000
In 1996, Anne Fagan, Story Landis, Barbacid and colleagues counted one ganglion at a

14
00:00:59.000 --> 00:00:60.000
series of ages.

15
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.620
It was the superior cervical ganglion, the sympathetic ganglion at the top of the

16
00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:06.620
neck.

17
00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:07.993
Here are the axes.

18
00:01:09.193 --> 00:01:10.713
Neuron number runs up the side.

19
00:01:11.673 --> 00:01:14.553
Embryonic and postnatal age runs along the bottom.

20
00:01:15.617 --> 00:01:21.937
Predict. If TrkA is needed for survival but not for production, what shape does the

21
00:01:21.937 --> 00:01:22.937
mutant curve take?

22
00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:34.470
Loss of TrkA did not affect neurogenesis, neuronal markers, or initial axon growth.

23
00:01:35.483 --> 00:01:40.983
In this schematic, the two counts match at embryonic day 13.5, soon after the

24
00:01:40.983 --> 00:01:41.983
ganglion forms.

25
00:01:42.783 --> 00:01:47.783
By embryonic day 15.5, the mutant ganglion already has fewer neurons.

26
00:01:48.703 --> 00:01:49.723
The gap keeps growing.

27
00:01:54.717 --> 00:01:57.397
The ganglion formed, and then lost its neurons.

28
00:01:58.337 --> 00:01:59.437
The neurons were produced.

29
00:02:00.337 --> 00:02:01.397
What failed was survival.

30
00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:07.187
This time course is the signature evidence that the loss is a failure of survival,

31
00:02:07.587 --> 00:02:08.587
not production.

32
00:02:09.317 --> 00:02:11.997
Counts of dividing and dying cells showed why.

33
00:02:12.837 --> 00:02:15.257
More neurons were dying, and division was normal.

34
00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.500
How does NGF hold off that death?

35
00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:23.080
Neurons that get too little die by a death that needs the protein Bax.

36
00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:28.293
Mice lacking Bax keep sympathetic neurons that would otherwise die.

37
00:02:29.133 --> 00:02:31.973
In culture, they survive when NGF is withdrawn.

38
00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:36.967
So NGF works by holding back a Bax dependent death program.

39
00:02:37.967 --> 00:02:42.247
Takeaway: without TrkA, sympathetic neurons are made and then lost.

40
00:02:43.147 --> 00:02:45.187
NGF acts as a survival factor.
